00:00:38.934 --> 00:00:40.847
- So because of the success
that I've had on social media

00:00:40.847 --> 00:00:43.784
I often get asked by people
who want to get their channels

00:00:43.784 --> 00:00:45.130
going and started.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:47.075
How do I have more success on my channels?

00:00:47.075 --> 00:00:49.178
How do I get more impact, more influence,

00:00:49.178 --> 00:00:50.314
help reach my goals?

00:00:50.314 --> 00:00:52.474
What's your advice on
what I should be doing?

00:00:52.474 --> 00:00:55.282
And so today I'm going
to share my seven ways,

00:00:55.282 --> 00:00:57.489
seven techniques for you to crush it

00:00:57.489 --> 00:00:59.989
in your niche on social media.

00:01:03.654 --> 00:01:05.914
Way number one is you have
to find the right platform.

00:01:05.914 --> 00:01:07.655
Find the best platform for you.

00:01:07.655 --> 00:01:09.418
And it starts with combining two things.

00:01:09.418 --> 00:01:12.454
One is what are your skills,
what are you really good at,

00:01:12.454 --> 00:01:14.599
what do you enjoy doing, what
do you want to get better at?

00:01:14.599 --> 00:01:16.532
So do you like being
in front of the camera,

00:01:16.532 --> 00:01:17.376
like I do?

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:20.676
Would you rather do podcasts
and just do audio only?

00:01:20.676 --> 00:01:23.051
Would you rather write, and
you can't stand the thought

00:01:23.051 --> 00:01:24.021
of being in front of a camera?

00:01:24.021 --> 00:01:26.961
Where do your skills line
up and the content that

00:01:26.961 --> 00:01:27.983
you're going to share?

00:01:27.983 --> 00:01:29.747
Are you a graphic designer,
do you want to create

00:01:29.747 --> 00:01:30.673
beautiful images?

00:01:30.673 --> 00:01:33.038
Are you a videographer, you
want to behind the camera,

00:01:33.038 --> 00:01:34.240
editing great things?

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.185
What are the skills you have?

00:01:36.185 --> 00:01:37.949
And combine it with
where are your customers?

00:01:37.949 --> 00:01:41.416
So for me, I love Youtube
because I get to be

00:01:41.416 --> 00:01:42.603
in front of the camera.

00:01:42.603 --> 00:01:44.074
It's where I have the most skills.

00:01:44.074 --> 00:01:47.392
I'd much rather make a video
than I would write a blog post.

00:01:47.392 --> 00:01:49.585
And I go to Youtube
because it's where most

00:01:49.585 --> 00:01:51.231
of my audience is.

00:01:51.231 --> 00:01:53.835
My audience are entrepreneurs,
or budding entrepreneurs,

00:01:53.835 --> 00:01:55.394
and wannabe entrepreneurs.

00:01:55.394 --> 00:01:57.446
And a lot of you guys are on Youtube.

00:01:57.446 --> 00:01:58.279
And you're watching.

00:01:58.279 --> 00:01:59.737
And so that combination works

00:01:59.737 --> 00:02:01.444
really really really well for me.

00:02:01.444 --> 00:02:04.310
It's why I've invested so
much of my time into Youtube

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.183
as opposed to the other platforms.

00:02:06.183 --> 00:02:08.846
And so understanding one,
what you're really good at,

00:02:08.846 --> 00:02:11.355
where your passion lies,
what skills you have,

00:02:11.355 --> 00:02:14.507
with two, where is your target market,

00:02:14.507 --> 00:02:15.750
where is your audience?

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.362
And then what platform,
which social media platform,

00:02:18.362 --> 00:02:21.987
performs the best across those two things.

00:02:21.987 --> 00:02:24.364
And I wouldn't try to do
every single social media

00:02:24.364 --> 00:02:25.426
platform to start.

00:02:25.426 --> 00:02:26.532
'Cause this is what happens,

00:02:26.532 --> 00:02:28.767
entrepreneurs try to do everything,

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:31.658
and then you end up doing nothing well.

00:02:31.658 --> 00:02:34.273
And you're posting crap to
all of these different places.

00:02:34.273 --> 00:02:35.977
So pick the one and start there.

00:02:35.977 --> 00:02:37.659
Pick the one that has the best results,

00:02:37.659 --> 00:02:39.288
the best potential results for you,

00:02:39.288 --> 00:02:42.621
and go all in on that one to start with.

00:02:44.511 --> 00:02:46.080
Number two is just start.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.037
A lot of people just don't start.

00:02:48.037 --> 00:02:51.888
You have an idea, one day I'm
going to start a Youtube channel.

00:02:51.888 --> 00:02:54.109
I have this big vision
for what I want to do,

00:02:54.109 --> 00:02:55.998
but you don't actually do anything.

00:02:55.998 --> 00:02:59.174
And this is where your
perfectionism can be a problem.

00:02:59.174 --> 00:03:00.445
A lot of people, they don't want to start

00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:01.492
until it's perfect.

00:03:01.492 --> 00:03:03.182
They need to have the perfect channel art

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.738
and to have the perfect setup,
you need the perfect gear.

00:03:05.738 --> 00:03:07.849
You need the perfect logo,
I need the perfect name.

00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:09.284
All this stuff has to be perfect,

00:03:09.284 --> 00:03:10.862
and because you want it to be perfect,

00:03:10.862 --> 00:03:12.253
you don't do anything.

00:03:12.253 --> 00:03:13.862
You never actually take any action.

00:03:13.862 --> 00:03:15.615
You just live in your
head of this future thing

00:03:15.615 --> 00:03:16.634
that you want to do.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.313
And so if you want to do it, just start.

00:03:18.313 --> 00:03:21.337
Start, expect it to be crap, it's okay

00:03:21.337 --> 00:03:23.331
'cause nobody is paying
attention to you yet.

00:03:23.331 --> 00:03:24.463
You're just getting started.

00:03:24.463 --> 00:03:26.047
You don't have a ton of
followers that you're going to

00:03:26.047 --> 00:03:27.049
mess up with.

00:03:27.049 --> 00:03:29.129
Just start and make it better the next day

00:03:29.129 --> 00:03:31.339
and better the next day
and better the next day.

00:03:31.339 --> 00:03:33.283
As soon as you get any kind of idea,

00:03:33.283 --> 00:03:35.300
the best thing you can
do is take some kind

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.156
of immediate action towards
achieving your goal.

00:03:38.156 --> 00:03:40.624
Whether it's social media
or any other kind of goal.

00:03:40.624 --> 00:03:41.860
Immediate action.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.721
You get an idea, just start.

00:03:43.721 --> 00:03:46.543
Do something immediately,
right away, right now.

00:03:46.543 --> 00:03:48.521
If it's a social media platform
that you're interested in,

00:03:48.521 --> 00:03:50.982
you want to start a
Youtube channel, start it.

00:03:50.982 --> 00:03:53.389
Go to Youtube, create
your account and record

00:03:53.389 --> 00:03:54.591
a video today.

00:03:54.591 --> 00:03:57.044
Expect it to be terrible,
expect it to be garbage.

00:03:57.044 --> 00:03:58.857
That's okay, it's your first video.

00:03:58.857 --> 00:04:00.712
Just make tomorrow's better.

00:04:00.712 --> 00:04:01.629
Just start.

00:04:05.249 --> 00:04:06.665
Number three is model success.

00:04:06.665 --> 00:04:09.054
Anytime you don't know
how to do something,

00:04:09.054 --> 00:04:10.874
the best thing you can
do is look for somebody

00:04:10.874 --> 00:04:12.641
who's already accomplished
what you want to do

00:04:12.641 --> 00:04:14.381
and look at the steps that they took.

00:04:14.381 --> 00:04:15.880
And you can look at where they're at now,

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.993
but you can also look at their journey

00:04:17.993 --> 00:04:20.563
and the path that they
took and learn from them.

00:04:20.563 --> 00:04:22.471
So for Youtube as an example,

00:04:22.471 --> 00:04:24.013
there's a number of
people that I look up to

00:04:24.013 --> 00:04:25.337
that I've learned from.

00:04:25.337 --> 00:04:27.218
I love watching Gary Vaynerchuk's channel,

00:04:27.218 --> 00:04:28.787
I love watching Lewis Howes's channel.

00:04:28.787 --> 00:04:31.584
There's a number of other
channels that I look up to,

00:04:31.584 --> 00:04:32.539
I learned a ton from.

00:04:32.539 --> 00:04:35.195
Tim Shmoyer, Derral Eves,
on how to build a proper

00:04:35.195 --> 00:04:37.857
Youtube channel, and the right
things to do, and strategies.

00:04:37.857 --> 00:04:40.198
And so I'd be constantly
looking for people

00:04:40.198 --> 00:04:43.484
that I can learn from in your industry.

00:04:43.484 --> 00:04:45.374
So if you want to be big on Youtube,

00:04:45.374 --> 00:04:47.678
if you want to be big on
Instagram, or big on Twitter,

00:04:47.678 --> 00:04:48.803
or big on LinkedIn,

00:04:48.803 --> 00:04:51.033
look at the people who
are already crushing it,

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:53.454
understand their path, break it down.

00:04:53.454 --> 00:04:55.029
Go back on their history
and their timeline

00:04:55.029 --> 00:04:57.669
and try to do a research to understand

00:04:57.669 --> 00:05:00.545
what were the things that they
did to achieve their success.

00:05:00.545 --> 00:05:02.283
And what I love looking at most is

00:05:02.283 --> 00:05:04.071
what was the turning point for them?

00:05:04.071 --> 00:05:06.098
What was the breaking
point that turned them from

00:05:06.098 --> 00:05:09.505
just someone who was doing
okay to really crushing it.

00:05:09.505 --> 00:05:10.811
And if you look at that,

00:05:10.811 --> 00:05:13.406
for a lot of different
people in your field,

00:05:13.406 --> 00:05:15.674
you'll get enough of an
idea what you need to do

00:05:15.674 --> 00:05:17.091
to be successful.

00:05:19.442 --> 00:05:22.427
Tip number four is be a storyteller.

00:05:22.427 --> 00:05:24.731
The reason you want to be
a storyteller is so that

00:05:24.731 --> 00:05:27.669
people can relate to you on a human level.

00:05:27.669 --> 00:05:30.116
When they do that, it's
not the product anymore

00:05:30.116 --> 00:05:32.545
that it's about, but the story behind it.

00:05:32.545 --> 00:05:34.461
And what that means is
that they're more inclined

00:05:34.461 --> 00:05:37.186
to follow you on social media,
to purchase your products

00:05:37.186 --> 00:05:39.119
and to promote it to their friends.

00:05:39.119 --> 00:05:41.374
Because they identify with you.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.515
So for example, me personally,

00:05:42.515 --> 00:05:46.415
I am on Snapchat, I am on
Instagram, I am on Facebook.

00:05:46.415 --> 00:05:48.831
Whenever I do posts, it's not
just a matter of me saying,

00:05:48.831 --> 00:05:52.076
hey guys, here are the
prices for all the classes

00:05:52.076 --> 00:05:53.060
coming up.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:55.280
Hey guys, here is a brand new social.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.771
You should come out and dance.

00:05:56.771 --> 00:06:00.114
I let clients, customers and friends

00:06:00.114 --> 00:06:02.698
make sure that they can
see the behind the scenes

00:06:02.698 --> 00:06:04.666
of what I do day to day,

00:06:04.666 --> 00:06:07.870
which helps them relate to me,
which helps them bond with me

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:10.378
and ultimately gives more
value than just the thing

00:06:10.378 --> 00:06:12.442
that we offer at the school.

00:06:12.442 --> 00:06:16.075
As a result, people are reaching
out and joining our school

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.947
when they've never even
heard of it except through

00:06:17.947 --> 00:06:20.254
the social media, where
they watch the Snaps,

00:06:20.254 --> 00:06:22.210
where they watch the Instagram posts

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:23.588
or where they're on Facebook.

00:06:23.588 --> 00:06:27.029
Ultimately, there are a lot
of ways to reach your clients.

00:06:27.029 --> 00:06:30.007
But altogether, you want
to make sure that again,

00:06:30.007 --> 00:06:32.444
you're a storyteller and
you are not just promoting

00:06:32.444 --> 00:06:35.444
the product or niche that you're in.

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:39.880
Tip number five is do collabs.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:42.307
One of the fastest way
to grow your presence

00:06:42.307 --> 00:06:45.184
and audience in a niche
is to do collaborations

00:06:45.184 --> 00:06:47.022
with people who are already in your niche,

00:06:47.022 --> 00:06:48.700
serving the same audience.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.670
Now they may not be exact
competitors of yours,

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:52.576
because you have your
message, they have theirs.

00:06:52.576 --> 00:06:54.501
But if you're targeting the same people,

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:57.810
and you can provide some
kind of value to them,

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.053
then it's a great opportunity
for you to be able

00:07:00.053 --> 00:07:02.181
to build up your
influence in your network.

00:07:02.181 --> 00:07:04.489
One of the first people
I did a collaboration

00:07:04.489 --> 00:07:07.327
with Tim Schmoyer, he has a
channel called Video Creators.

00:07:07.327 --> 00:07:09.906
And, again, I mentioned
I love that channel.

00:07:09.906 --> 00:07:12.565
I used it a lot to learn
how to build up my channel.

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:15.072
And I was a big fan of what he did

00:07:15.072 --> 00:07:16.803
and I reached out and we connected.

00:07:16.803 --> 00:07:18.724
I said, hey, I'd love to
be a part of your channel.

00:07:18.724 --> 00:07:20.741
Here are some ideas that I could present

00:07:20.741 --> 00:07:22.507
that I think would be of interest to you

00:07:22.507 --> 00:07:25.060
and really provide some
value to your audience.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:26.993
And we picked one and
that was the first piece

00:07:26.993 --> 00:07:28.795
of content that went up.

00:07:28.795 --> 00:07:31.232
And it was great, because
Tim's audience is entrepreneurs

00:07:31.232 --> 00:07:34.243
but Tim will teach people how
to build a Youtube channel.

00:07:34.243 --> 00:07:36.449
And I'll teach people
how to be entrepreneurs.

00:07:36.449 --> 00:07:39.114
And so, I'm not sharing
the exact same advice

00:07:39.114 --> 00:07:40.209
that Tim is.

00:07:40.209 --> 00:07:42.725
And so, I went on his
channel, he eventually came

00:07:42.725 --> 00:07:43.577
on my channel.

00:07:43.577 --> 00:07:46.855
I think I've done three or
more collabs on Tim's channel.

00:07:46.855 --> 00:07:49.219
I just came back from
Climber Con in Palm Springs.

00:07:49.219 --> 00:07:50.381
Met other Youtubers.

00:07:50.381 --> 00:07:52.184
Ended up doing four or five
different collaborations

00:07:52.184 --> 00:07:54.055
on different people's channels.

00:07:54.055 --> 00:07:55.881
So if you're reaching
out to do collaborations,

00:07:55.881 --> 00:07:59.093
the ideal people are the ones
that you already know of.

00:07:59.093 --> 00:08:00.437
You've already consumed their content.

00:08:00.437 --> 00:08:02.572
You already know what message
is going to hit for them.

00:08:02.572 --> 00:08:04.074
You're a fan of their channel.

00:08:04.074 --> 00:08:05.575
You engage in their channel.

00:08:05.575 --> 00:08:08.406
Ideally, you want to be a known quantity.

00:08:08.406 --> 00:08:10.130
You've left comments on their videos,

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.358
you've engaged with them on Twitter.

00:08:11.358 --> 00:08:14.980
You've connected somehow in a
little bit of a back and forth

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:16.424
so that when you reach out and say,

00:08:16.424 --> 00:08:17.801
hey, I'd love to do a collaboration,

00:08:17.801 --> 00:08:19.349
here are some ideas I have,

00:08:19.349 --> 00:08:21.954
they already know who
you are because not maybe

00:08:21.954 --> 00:08:23.200
of the great content you've put up,

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:24.497
'cause maybe you're just getting started,

00:08:24.497 --> 00:08:26.535
but because of the
interaction that you have

00:08:26.535 --> 00:08:28.038
already made with them.

00:08:28.038 --> 00:08:29.563
And that's easy to do,
it's just providing value

00:08:29.563 --> 00:08:31.556
on what they're already doing.

00:08:31.556 --> 00:08:34.289
So if they're big on Twitter,
respond to them on Twitter.

00:08:34.289 --> 00:08:36.065
If they're big on Youtube,
make a comment on every

00:08:36.065 --> 00:08:36.905
single video.

00:08:36.905 --> 00:08:39.497
You should be a known quantity to them

00:08:39.497 --> 00:08:41.502
before you reach out to
make a collaboration.

00:08:41.502 --> 00:08:43.808
Once you do, collaborations
are one of the best

00:08:43.808 --> 00:08:47.058
ways you will quickly grow an audience.

00:08:49.338 --> 00:08:50.861
Tip number six is build a team.

00:08:50.861 --> 00:08:53.066
At the start, you got to
do everything yourself.

00:08:53.066 --> 00:08:54.630
I'm a big believer in not spending money

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:55.748
until you're making money.

00:08:55.748 --> 00:08:57.446
So I do everything myself.

00:08:57.446 --> 00:08:59.022
When I first started this Youtube channel,

00:08:59.022 --> 00:09:00.294
I did everything.

00:09:00.294 --> 00:09:02.201
I was in front of the camera,
I was behind the camera,

00:09:02.201 --> 00:09:03.462
I was editing, I was researching,

00:09:03.462 --> 00:09:06.702
I was doing the SCO, I was
do everything for my channel.

00:09:06.702 --> 00:09:09.759
And because of that, I
was doing a video a month

00:09:09.759 --> 00:09:11.169
to a video a week.

00:09:11.169 --> 00:09:12.857
That was the max that I could do.

00:09:12.857 --> 00:09:15.295
As I started earning some more money,

00:09:15.295 --> 00:09:17.378
I said, okay, I'm getting
serious about this.

00:09:17.378 --> 00:09:19.205
I want to start to build a team.

00:09:19.205 --> 00:09:21.392
And the first person I hired was somebody

00:09:21.392 --> 00:09:22.480
to do my editing.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:24.907
Because I hated it, and
I was super slow at it.

00:09:24.907 --> 00:09:26.895
And that allowed me to
go from a video a week

00:09:26.895 --> 00:09:28.262
to a video a day.

00:09:28.262 --> 00:09:30.513
Just hiring somebody to
do the editing for me.

00:09:30.513 --> 00:09:32.816
I got to spend more
time doing what I love.

00:09:32.816 --> 00:09:35.165
He was way better at
doing the editing anyway.

00:09:35.165 --> 00:09:37.274
And my channel started to lift and grow.

00:09:37.274 --> 00:09:39.816
Now I've got eight people who
work on my Youtube channel.

00:09:39.816 --> 00:09:43.489
It allows me to make three videos a day.

00:09:43.489 --> 00:09:46.878
Because of the people that
I've surrounded myself with,

00:09:46.878 --> 00:09:48.513
I'm able to put out more content

00:09:48.513 --> 00:09:51.257
and I'm able to spend my
time doing what I think

00:09:51.257 --> 00:09:54.522
I'm great at and not worry
about everything else

00:09:54.522 --> 00:09:56.709
that's associated with
building up my channel.

00:09:56.709 --> 00:09:59.296
And so, at the start,
you start at the start.

00:09:59.296 --> 00:10:00.330
You do everything yourself.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:03.498
You can't compare yourself
to where somebody else is at

00:10:03.498 --> 00:10:04.362
in their middle.

00:10:04.362 --> 00:10:06.522
So you start at the start,
you do everything yourself.

00:10:06.522 --> 00:10:07.794
But quickly start to think about

00:10:07.794 --> 00:10:10.039
what is it that you are
great at and where you want

00:10:10.039 --> 00:10:11.178
to spend your time at,

00:10:11.178 --> 00:10:13.218
and as soon as you start making
some money on the channel,

00:10:13.218 --> 00:10:15.631
on any social media channel
that you're working on,

00:10:15.631 --> 00:10:16.734
start to think about,

00:10:16.734 --> 00:10:18.798
okay, as soon as I
start making some money,

00:10:18.798 --> 00:10:21.212
this is the first person
I'm going to hire.

00:10:21.212 --> 00:10:22.663
Start thinking immediately
that you're planning

00:10:22.663 --> 00:10:25.806
to hire people to turn
this into a business,

00:10:25.806 --> 00:10:29.889
will allow you to focus
on what you are great at.

00:10:31.934 --> 00:10:34.866
And tip number seven, and
probably my most important tip

00:10:34.866 --> 00:10:36.283
is be consistent.

00:10:37.408 --> 00:10:40.374
So many of you guys are
not consistent enough

00:10:40.374 --> 00:10:41.657
to have success.

00:10:41.657 --> 00:10:42.728
It's a real problem.

00:10:42.728 --> 00:10:45.184
If you look at my channel,
why has my Youtube channel

00:10:45.184 --> 00:10:46.122
grown so much?

00:10:46.122 --> 00:10:48.423
I've made over 5,000 videos.

00:10:48.423 --> 00:10:50.835
Only 4,000 of them are public.

00:10:50.835 --> 00:10:53.983
We've got 1,000 non-public
just practice videos

00:10:53.983 --> 00:10:55.868
that I put up on my channel.

00:10:55.868 --> 00:10:57.401
5,000 videos.

00:10:57.401 --> 00:10:59.383
I wasn't very good at the start.

00:10:59.383 --> 00:11:01.615
If you go back on my channel
and look at my earlier videos,

00:11:01.615 --> 00:11:04.062
you'll see that I wasn't very good.

00:11:04.062 --> 00:11:05.610
I wasn't very comfortable, I was nervous,

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:07.910
I was stuttering, I was
trying to find my path.

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:10.288
It wasn't very good.

00:11:10.288 --> 00:11:12.330
And with more practice, and as I did more,

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:15.608
I got better and it also
trains the audience.

00:11:15.608 --> 00:11:18.063
People come when they
expect to get more content

00:11:18.063 --> 00:11:20.229
and it plays well with
the Youtube algorithm

00:11:20.229 --> 00:11:23.175
or whatever algorithm you're
posting to on social media.

00:11:23.175 --> 00:11:24.618
You need to be consistent.

00:11:24.618 --> 00:11:28.831
And so so many people start
and they make one video,

00:11:28.831 --> 00:11:30.506
or they make one piece of content.

00:11:30.506 --> 00:11:32.672
And that's it, and they fall off.

00:11:32.672 --> 00:11:33.919
And the next week,
maybe they make one more

00:11:33.919 --> 00:11:35.250
and they fall back down.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.162
The next week ...

00:11:36.162 --> 00:11:37.494
You got to put it in your calendar.

00:11:37.494 --> 00:11:41.130
If you want to crush it
in anything that you do,

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:43.339
it's the topic, how are we going
to crush it on social media.

00:11:43.339 --> 00:11:45.332
If you want to crush it
in anything that you do,

00:11:45.332 --> 00:11:46.816
you have to spend the time.

00:11:46.816 --> 00:11:49.071
You got to dedicate the
time to make it great.

00:11:49.071 --> 00:11:50.046
Yes, there are shortcuts.

00:11:50.046 --> 00:11:51.282
Yes, you can model success.

00:11:51.282 --> 00:11:52.518
Yes, you can get there faster.

00:11:52.518 --> 00:11:54.435
But you still have to spend the time.

00:11:54.435 --> 00:11:55.494
It's not just going to happen.

00:11:55.494 --> 00:11:56.695
You're not going to turn on the camera

00:11:56.695 --> 00:11:59.798
and just be amazing and get
five million subscribers.

00:11:59.798 --> 00:12:01.928
You got to be consistent.

00:12:01.928 --> 00:12:05.275
And so look at your calendar
and factor in the time,

00:12:05.275 --> 00:12:08.114
either every day or a big
chunk of time every week

00:12:08.114 --> 00:12:11.789
to spend on your social media,
creating better content.

00:12:11.789 --> 00:12:14.514
And I'm a firm believer
that the quantity leads

00:12:14.514 --> 00:12:15.775
to the quality.

00:12:15.775 --> 00:12:20.035
The quality is what's
going to get you the base,

00:12:20.035 --> 00:12:22.899
the subscribers, the brand deals,

00:12:22.899 --> 00:12:24.750
the attention, the impact.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:25.912
It's the quality content.

00:12:25.912 --> 00:12:28.759
But to get to the quality,
you have to produce

00:12:28.759 --> 00:12:30.510
a ton of quantity.

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:32.047
Just like anything else.

00:12:32.047 --> 00:12:34.689
To get the muscles, you have
to lift a lot of weights.

00:12:34.689 --> 00:12:36.647
To get good at a language,
you have to practice

00:12:36.647 --> 00:12:38.250
over and over and over again.

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.227
The quantity leads to the quality.

00:12:40.227 --> 00:12:43.109
And so you need to be
consistent in your output.

00:12:43.109 --> 00:12:45.086
So these are my seven tips on what to do

00:12:45.086 --> 00:12:47.681
to crush it in your niche on social media.

00:12:47.681 --> 00:12:49.614
I'd love to know, what did you guys think?

00:12:49.614 --> 00:12:50.672
What was your favorite rule?

00:12:50.672 --> 00:12:53.132
Is there an eight, nine, 10 that
you want to add to the list?

00:12:53.132 --> 00:12:54.716
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:12:54.716 --> 00:12:55.854
